  "title": "Lemon Rosemary Salmon",
  "description": null,
  "editorial": {
    "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Tasty, simple and beautiful looking dish for everyday or special occasions. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:wp-recipe-maker/recipe {\"id\":21478,\"template\":\"chic-template-english\",\"updated\":1656289305160} -->\n<!--WPRM Recipe 21478-->\n<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe\">\n\t<h2 class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-name\">Lemon Rosemary Salmon</h2>\n\t<img class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-image\" src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/received_10211398235933985.Blog_-1-150x150.png\"/>\t<p class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-summary\">\n\t\t\t</p>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-equipment\">\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-ingredients\">\n\t\t<ul><li>4 salmon fillets (remove bone and skin)</li><li>1 large  lemon (thinly sliced )</li><li>8 spring fresh rosemary (washed)</li><li>8 Tbsp olive oil</li><li>salt and pepper (to taste)</li><li>1 tsp paprika</li></ul>\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-instructions\">\n\t\t<ol><li>Preheat oven to 350ºF.</li><li>Add 4 Tbsp of olive oil to baking dish. Place one slice of lemon and one rosemary spring under each salmon fillet.  </li><li>Add salt, pepper and paprika evenly over salmon and place one slice of lemon and one rosemary spring on top of salmon.</li><li>Drizzle 4 Tbsp of olive oil over salmon.  <br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/received_10211398232653903.Blog_-1-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li>Bake 25 minutes until salmon is flaky.</li><li>Place salmon on serving platter and enjoy.  </li></ol>\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-notes\">\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-meta\">\n\t\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-meta-course\">Main Dish</div>\t</div>\n</div>\n<!--End WPRM Recipe-->\n<!-- /wp:wp-recipe-maker/recipe -->",
    "excerpt": null
  },
